  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want messages to keep loading after I change the in-app text size, so that adjusting readability never leaves me on an endless \"Chargement des messages\".\n\n### Report\nOperator, device test 2026-11-11 (iPhone, `dev-swift` `f74710d0`): after changing the app text size in the settings from **100 to 90** (LOT-169, app-wide text size, #391), messages no longer load, in topics **and in MP conversations** (MPs otherwise load on this build, see #750).\n\n### Scope\n- Find the cause: whether the setting change rebuilds or reloads the reader (environment change, view identity, web view reload) and hits the same stuck-load race as #750 / #643, or something else. Measure, do not assume.\n- If it shares #750's cause, the #750 fix (running as `mac/i750`) covers it with its own test; otherwise a separate fix.\n- The #750 load timeout must also cover it: a load that never ends turns into the failure banner with \"Réessayer\".\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] With a topic and an MP open (and in the background), changing the text size (100 → 90 → 110) keeps their messages shown, or reloads them, every time.\n- [ ] Opening a topic or an MP after a text-size change loads its messages.\n- [ ] A test fails without the fix.\n- [ ] Checked on device by the operator.\n\nRelated: #750 (stuck reopen, topics), #643 (MP second conversation), #391 (LOT-169).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
